      "status": "preserved"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0001",
      "source": "The translation aspect of this matrix indicates the position of the center of the eyeball, relative to the position represented by the anchor’s [`transform`](aranchor/transform.md).",
      "ko": "이 행렬의 translation 구성 요소는 앵커의 [`transform`](aranchor/transform.md)으로 표시되는 위치를 기준으로 눈알 중심의 위치를 나타냅니다.",
      "sourceHash": "3b90192a0b0f5084b7986de6ace5e5967283027a0a1e5d3167ac80f73f93b9fb",
      "status": "machine_translated"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0002",
      "source": "The positive z-axis points from the center of the eyeball in the direction of the pupil.",
      "ko": "양의 z축은 눈알 중심에서 동공 방향으로 향합니다.",
      "sourceHash": "d2179d5ffd9a35a01292c01e5d8892eee00e857cc988ba7455bb3be73db3514a",
      "status": "machine_translated"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0009:0001",
      "source": "Rotational aspects of the matrix indicate the orientation of the eyeball—for example, a rotation about the x-axis directs the pupil upward or downward.",
      "ko": "Identify the anchors you want to react to by calling [`id`](anchor/id.md).",
      "sourceHash": "af178aaf82c13b2b983f74dd2f77f7ff4c12d4bb28734735ea41f39434d0bb16",
      "status": "machine_translated"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0009:0002",
      "source": "The eye does not rotate about the z-axis.",
      "ko": "눈은 z축을 기준으로 회전하지 않습니다.",
      "sourceHash": "220945deddfa6913422f85014715e182f69eac0bdbee78bd04d40f61ac35a86f",
      "status": "machine_translated"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0010:0001",
      "source": "![Diagram showing the coordinate axis origin defined by the rightEyeTransform, representing both the position and rotation of the eye relative to the face anchor.](https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/3a144016a0f37954454fcd4e6c20a9c3/media-3001544%402x.png)",
      "ko": "![Diagram showing the coordinate axis origin defined by the rightEyeTransform, representing both the position and rotation of the eye relative to the face anchor.](https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/3a144016a0f37954454fcd4e6c20a9c3/media-3001544%402x.png)",
